-- every control this platform offers --
  each one did exactly what was promised: true
  corners were taken by all of them or none: true
  and so were borders: true
-- the four that draw their own background --
  every one of them refused: true
  and everything else took one: true
  there are four of them wherever a platform dresses: true
-- the five that draw text a program can colour --
  exactly the ones that should took one: true
  and there are five of them: true
  which is fewer than every control offered: true
-- a text colour reads back, and the wrong control is named --
  the colour that went in: true
  a progress bar has no text to colour: true
  and the refusal names it: true
-- the one everybody expects to fail --
  a push button takes a background: true
-- and the refusal names the control --
  a text field is always refused one: true
  and told which control and why: true
  a negative radius is refused everywhere: true
-- and what was set reads back --
  the corner radius that went in: true
  the border width that went in: true
  and the colour, byte for byte: true
  one nobody dressed reads zero: true
-- and markup dresses a control the same way --
  the colour written in markup is the control's: true
  a colour that is not one is refused at render: true
